  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 215 AM EDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nPattern Synopsis and Forecast:\n\nWarm advection begins to overspread the region later today, \nalong with mid level moisture as a short wave digs into the \nUpper Midwest. Consequently, a few showers may be possible this \nafternoon/evening across the E UP. The main lift from that \napproaching s/w coupled with better column moisture will move \ninto the area later tonight into the middle portions of Sunday, \ncoinciding with the best chance for showers. Generally a light \nrainfall for many. Otherwise, much of the day on Saturday will \nbe quiet and pleasant, a few degrees warmer than Friday.\n\nFirst push of cooler air will be Sunday afternoon as winds \nbecome breezy and shift to the northwest. Thus, despite some \nelevated winds, temperatures will be relatively cool/cold Sunday\nnight with low to mid 30s possible, with another round of frost\nproducts not out of the question. High pressure settles and \noozes into northern MI Monday and Monday night with slackening \nwinds and mostly clear skies, setting the stage for the coldest \nnight of the fall season. A freeze is likely for many away from \nthe immediate shorelines.\n\nSubtle hint at a few lake induced rain showers Sunday \nafternoon/Sunday night by some pieces of ensemble guidance prior\nto the sfc high pressure moving into the region. Nevertheless, \nmuch of early next week will be cool (Monday) and dry. Heading \ninto the mid to later portions of next week, deep troughing will\nhang out just to the north of the region across Ontario and \nadjacent Canadian provinces, with occasional features embedded \nwithin the main flow trying to impinge across northern Michigan.\nConsequently, although right now it looks more dry than wet \nduring this time period, occasional light shower chances cannot \nbe ruled out, especially the farther north one is. Little bit of\na rebound as well temperature wise with 60s during this time, \nalthough well keep an eye on this moving forward.",
